{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2174-04-12 22:43:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, I'm Dr. Lee, one of the hospitalists. You're here because of a severe headache. Can you tell me more about it?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2174-04-12 22:45:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, it started yesterday in the back of my head and now it’s all over. It feels just like my usual flare-ups when my psoriatic arthritis gets worse."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2174-04-12 22:47:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You mentioned you tried morphine at home. Did it help at all?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2174-04-12 22:48:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I took my regular dose—30 mg twice and 15 mg twice—but it didn’t touch the pain. That’s when I called rheumatology, and they told me to come in."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2174-04-12 22:50:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Okay, thanks. No fever, neck stiffness, or vision changes?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2174-04-12 22:51:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "No, none of that. Just the headache and some swelling in my hands and feet, which also happens when my disease flares."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2174-04-12 22:53:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Got it. In the ER, you got IV morphine and steroids. How’s the pain now compared to earlier?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2174-04-12 22:55:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Better, but still there. The IV meds helped a lot, but I know it’ll come back if we don’t do something."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2174-04-12 22:57:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll keep you on your prednisone and azathioprine. The rheumatology team reviewed your case and doesn’t think increasing steroids will help long-term."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2174-04-12 22:59:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That makes sense. I’ve been on prednisone for over a year now. I’m just waiting on approval for Humira, but it’s taking forever."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2174-04-12 23:01:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see. The pain team is also involved. They’re thinking about an occipital nerve block tomorrow to help break this cycle."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2174-04-12 23:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve heard of that. Is it safe? I’ve had Botox before, but it never got approved for me this time."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2174-04-12 23:05:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, it’s very safe. They’ll inject a numbing medicine and a steroid around the nerves at the base of your skull. It often gives good relief for cervicogenic headaches like yours."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2174-04-12 23:07:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, I’m willing to try it. My headaches are always worse when my immune suppression is low."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2174-04-12 23:09:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. And we’re not seeing signs of infection—no fever or meningismus—so this seems like a flare, not something new."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2174-04-12 23:11:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good. I also started Augmentin for an axillary abscess a few days ago. Is that okay to keep taking?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2174-04-12 23:13:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we’ll continue that for the full 7-day course. No signs of spreading infection."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2174-04-13 08:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. How’s your headache today?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2174-04-13 08:17:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Still there, but maybe a little less intense. I slept okay after the last dose of morphine."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2174-04-13 08:19:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your labs from last night were stable. White count is normal, though neutrophils are high, which we expect from long-term steroid use."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2174-04-13 08:21:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Makes sense. I’ve had that before. What’s the plan for today?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2174-04-13 08:23:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re scheduling the nerve block for tomorrow morning. In the meantime, we’ll keep your pain managed with oral morphine and monitor your response."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2174-04-13 08:25:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my diabetes? I’m on glargine and sliding scale. Should I keep that up?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2174-04-13 08:27:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, continue glargine 50 in the morning and 30 at night. We’re holding glyburide for now since steroids can raise your blood sugar."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2174-04-13 08:29:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. And my blood pressure meds—Toprol, HCTZ, lisinopril—I should keep those too?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2174-04-13 08:31:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, continue all your usual meds except glyburide. We’re also keeping your Bactrim for PJP prevention because of your immunosuppression."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2174-04-13 14:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The pain team confirmed—the nerve block is scheduled for tomorrow at noon."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2174-04-13 14:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Great. Any restrictions before the procedure?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2174-04-13 14:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Just stay on your regular diet. They’ll use local anesthesia, so no fasting needed. You’ll be awake but comfortable."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2174-04-14 12:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The nerve block is about to start. They’ll inject numbing medicine and a steroid into the occipital nerves on both sides."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2174-04-14 12:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, I’m ready. I hope this helps."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2174-04-14 12:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "All done. No complications. You’ll start to feel relief in a few hours, though it might take a day or two for full effect."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2174-04-14 12:17:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I already feel a bit looser in the neck. That’s promising."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2174-04-14 12:20:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good sign. We’re discharging you today. Your pain is stable on oral meds, and you’re otherwise doing well."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2174-04-14 12:22:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "What changes to my meds? I saw some adjustments in the list."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2174-04-14 12:24:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re cutting some doses—like lowering your metoprolol and HCTZ—because your blood pressure has been stable. Prednisone stays at 50 mg daily."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2174-04-14 12:26:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And the morphine?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2174-04-14 12:28:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ll go home with sustained-release morphine every 12 hours and the immediate-release as needed. Take it as prescribed, and don’t drive while on it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2174-04-14 12:30:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Understood. Should I follow up with pain clinic again?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2174-04-14 12:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, especially if headaches return. The nerve block may help, but long-term, the pain clinic can explore other options like Botox if approved."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2174-04-14 12:34:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And rheumatology?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2174-04-14 12:36:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Continue working on getting Humira approved. No changes to your azathioprine or other meds."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2174-04-14 12:38:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "What about the Augmentin?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2174-04-14 12:40:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Finish the full course—four more days. It’s for the recurring axillary abscess, and we want to make sure it clears."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2174-04-14 12:42:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my blood sugar checks?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2174-04-14 12:44:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Keep doing four fingersticks a day. Resume glyburide as planned unless your sugars run low."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2174-04-14 12:46:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I feel ready to go home. Thanks for getting me through this flare."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2174-04-14 12:48:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. Call your doctor if headaches worsen or aren’t controlled. Otherwise, follow up as scheduled."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2174-04-14 12:50:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will do. Appreciate all the help."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2174-04-14 12:52:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Take care. You’ll be discharged in the next hour."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2174-04-12 22:43:00",
    "admission_end": "2174-04-14 13:22:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "A 50-year-old male with psoriatic arthritis on chronic immunosuppression was admitted for an acute exacerbation of cervicogenic headache. The headache, consistent with prior flares, began in the occipital region and generalized, unresponsive to home morphine. He was treated in the ED with IV morphine and solumedrol, then transitioned to oral pain medications. Rheumatology recommended no steroid dose change. The pain service performed a bilateral greater occipital nerve block with bupivacaine and steroid, after which pain improved. He continued on prednisone, azathioprine, and Augmentin for an axillary abscess. Diabetes management included holding glyburide and continuing insulin. He was discharged home with stable pain, medication adjustments, and follow-up planned with pain and rheumatology clinics.",
    "problems": [
      "Headache",
      "Cellulitis and abscess of upper arm and forearm",
      "Psoriatic arthropathy",
      "Diabetes mellitus without mention of complication, type II or unspecified type, uncontrolled",
      "Other chronic pain",
      "Unspecified essential hypertension",
      "Other and unspecified noninfectious gastroenteritis and colitis",
      "Other and unspecified hyperlipidemia",
      "Obstructive sleep apnea (adult)(pediatric)",
      "Restless legs syndrome (RLS)",
      "Cornea replaced by transplant",
      "Other specified disorders of sweat glands",
      "Unspecified hereditary and idiopathic peripheral neuropathy",
      "Other chronic nonalcoholic liver disease"
    ]
  }
}
